.TH DDPAR-RESTORE 1 "2026-10-17" "ddpar 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ddpar-restore \- restore a segmented ddpar backup
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ddpar-restore
.BI \-i " backup-base"
.BI \-o " destination"
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Validate backup metadata and parts before restoring to a local file or block
device. Worker count and block size come from the backup metadata.
The command is also available as ddpar-restore.sh.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-i " base" ", \-\-input " base
Backup basename including its path, without the \-metadata.txt or part suffix.
The backup is remote when \-r or \-R is used.
.TP
.BI \-o " path" ", \-\-output " path
Local output file, block device or directory. A directory destination uses
the filename recorded in the metadata.
.TP
.BR \-r " [n|c]"
Enable remote restore (default: n). For compressed backups, mode n decompresses
locally, while mode c decompresses on the remote host. Mode l is rejected.
.TP
.BI \-R " [user@]host"
SSH host or SSH configuration alias containing the backup. Also enables remote
operation.
.TP
.B \-y
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.TP
.B \-P
Skip fallocate preallocation for a regular-file destination.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show built-in help.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DDPAR_NETWORK_TIMEOUT
Netcat inactivity timeout in seconds (default: 300).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ddpar-restore \-i /mnt/backups/sdb \-o /dev/sdc
ddpar-restore \-i /backup/disk \-o restored.img \-r c \-R user@host \-y
.fi
.SH NOTES
Restoration overwrites the destination. Regular files are truncated to the
saved size; block devices keep data beyond the saved image.
Incomplete backups and invalid part lengths are rejected. Compressed parts
are checked including gzip CRC; local SHA256 files are checked when available.
Remote payloads use unencrypted netcat; only the SSH control channel is
encrypted. Use remote transfers on trusted networks.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success; nonzero indicates an error or a refused operation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ddpar (1),
.BR ddpar-check (1)
